{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"7bda1b1bc357cfb57066a8836cecbf25b279d21dc912b27c9349eed1e8cef1b7","digest":{"component_or_area":"leaf-registry coverage testing","key_entities":["test_leaves_registry_coverage.py","_LEAVES registry","test_every_leaf_has_real_body","ApplyResult","mock Jira client","behavioral effect matrix"],"problem_keywords":["test coverage","leaf registry","behavioral validation","effect matrix","heuristic weakness","structural proxy","ast statements"],"propositions":["The current AST-based heuristic (≥3 statements or regex match) passes while leaves send wrong targets, drop fields, return wrong follow-ons, or swallow errors, failing to validate actual behavior.","A per-leaf behavioral effect matrix must be enumerated from _LEAVES itself, with a test asserting every leaf id has a matrix entry so newly-added uncovered leaves fail immediately.","Each matrix entry must assert observable effects with specificity: exact client/store method + argument, exact payload fields sent, exact ApplyResult returned, and follow-on calls, such that target, field, and follow-on defects are structurally caught.","Every leaf with an error/exception path must have assertions covering that failure behavior (exception type or error ApplyResult); leaves without error paths assert success ApplyResult.","Existing behavioral tests (e.g. test_apply_outbound_*) should be folded into or referenced by the matrix to avoid redundancy while achieving one complete enumerated behavioral matrix over _LEAVES."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825246406647396,"uuid":"35d88179-b1b5-435f-820a-8d2b1caa376f"}